From: emilyastranova <emily@astralabs.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: exit the sink state on CC only

The PM8150B Type-C state machine leaves Attached.SNK when VBUS drops out
of its 5 V window. A USB-PD source stepping to 9 V or 12 V takes VBUS
through that window, so the port reports a detach about 70 ms after the
Accept, TCPM restarts from SNK_UNATTACHED and the contract only completes
when PS_RDY happens to win the race. The stock driver sets
EXIT_SNK_BASED_ON_CC around PD resets so the sink state follows CC alone;
set it at init. TCPM already tolerates VBUS changes while a transition is
pending and detaches on CC.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c
@@ -702,7 +702,15 @@
 		goto done;
 
 	/* Set CC threshold to 1.6 Volts | tPDdebounce = 10-20ms */
-	mask = SEL_SRC_UPPER_REF | USE_TPD_FOR_EXITING_ATTACHSRC;
+	/*
+	 * Leave the sink state on CC alone. Otherwise the hardware state
+	 * machine exits Attached.SNK as soon as VBUS leaves its 5 V window,
+	 * which it does during a USB-PD voltage step and a hard reset; the
+	 * port reports a detach mid-transition and the contract never
+	 * completes. The stock driver sets the same bit around PD resets.
+	 */
+	mask = SEL_SRC_UPPER_REF | USE_TPD_FOR_EXITING_ATTACHSRC |
+	       EXIT_SNK_BASED_ON_CC;
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(pmic_typec_port->regmap,
 				 pmic_typec_port->base + TYPEC_EXIT_STATE_CFG_REG,
 				 mask, mask);
